# Gleanvolt settings for this machine.
#
# Anything in appsettings.json can be set here, one KEY=VALUE per line, with "__" (two underscores)
# between sections: Pv__Inverter__Host sets "Pv": { "Inverter": { "Host" } }. No quotes needed.
#
# This file is yours. Upgrades never overwrite it; `apt purge gleanvolt` is the only thing that
# removes it. After a change:
#
#   sudo systemctl restart gleanvolt
#
# and check it came up:
#
#   systemctl status gleanvolt
#   journalctl -u gleanvolt -e
#
# Every setting is described in the README: https://github.com/mpospisil/gleanvolt

# The PV system settings in sections 1 and 2 can also be edited in the web UI (PV system page, once a
# login is set in section 3). A value saved there goes to /var/lib/gleanvolt/pv-system.json and WINS
# over this file, key by key, until it is reverted on that page or the file is deleted.

# --- 1. Your inverter and charger -- change these first -------------------------------------------
# The defaults are the reference installation's addresses. On any other network nothing answers
# there and the dashboard stays empty. Both devices answer Modbus TCP on port 502, so a swapped pair
# looks like a frozen battery and zero solar rather than an error: check which is which.
#
#Pv__Inverter__Host=192.168.2.10
#Pv__Chargers__0__Host=192.168.2.6

# --- 2. The installation --------------------------------------------------------------------------
#Pv__Id=home-roof
#Pv__Name=Home Roof
#Pv__Latitude=50.0755
#Pv__Longitude=14.4378

# Usable capacity of the home battery, in kWh. The forecast-driven modes need it.
#ChargeControl__Forecast__BatteryCapacityKWh=9.0

# An IANA zone, if this machine's own zone is not the site's.
#Controller__TimeZone=Europe/Prague

# --- 3. The web UI --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# On by default at http://<this machine>:8090, plain HTTP and with NO LOGIN: anyone on the LAN can
# change the charging mode. To require a password, generate its hash and set it here:
#
#   /opt/gleanvolt/Gleanvolt.Worker hash-password 'your password'
#
#Web__PasswordHash=
#Web__Port=8090

# --- 4. Solar forecast (optional) -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Without a key, no forecast is fetched and the forecast-driven modes have nothing to plan with.
#Solcast__ApiKey=
#Solcast__ResourceId=

# --- 5. Battery discharge hold (optional, writes to the inverter) ---------------------------------
# Off, and dry-run when on, until you have checked the register addresses against your own device.
#BatteryHold__Enabled=true
#BatteryHold__DryRun=false
